# Open Energy Grid Explorer — Document Analysis & Clarification Questions

## ✅ Confirmed Understanding

### Scope
- **Single mock city** with a small, fixed set of assets — NOT a real GIS dataset
- A **visual exploration tool** (digital twin prototype), not a physics-accurate simulator
- No auth, no SCADA, no cloud, no paid APIs, no complex power flow math

### Tech Stack (LOCKED)
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React (Vite) |
| Map | Leaflet + OpenStreetMap tiles |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS + Lucide Icons |
| State | TanStack Query + Context API |
| Backend | FastAPI (Python 3.10+) |
| Data Store | JSON-based local storage |
| Simulation | Custom Python script |
| Charts | Recharts |

### Data Model — Assets
| Asset Type | Count | Key Attributes |
|---|---|---|
| Solar Farm | 1 | 50 MW, variable (time-of-day) |
| Gas Turbine (CCGT) | 1 | 150 MW, constant/stable |
| Transmission Lines | 3–5 | 110 kV, thick orange lines |
| Substations | 2 | Step-down 110kV → 11kV |
| Distribution Feeders | (implied) | 11 kV, thin blue lines |
| Hospital (Critical) | 1 | High priority |
| Data Center (Industrial) | 1 | Steady high load |
| Residential (Neighborhood) | 4–8 | Variable, evening peak |
| **Total consumers** | **6–10** | Mixed types |

### Simulation Engine
- Updates every **5 seconds**
- Data points per asset: **V, I, P, Q**
- Patterns: Diurnal cycles (solar output, residential load)
- Elastic rebalancing when solar drops (simplified)

### API Endpoints
| Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `GET /assets` | List all assets with coordinates |
| `GET /assets/{id}` | Detailed metadata for one asset |
| `GET /assets/{id}/metrics` | Latest values + last 1 hour history |
| `GET /network` | Adjacency list of connections |

### Frontend (Phase 2 — deferred)
- Full-screen Leaflet map, dark theme
- Layer control: High Voltage vs Low Voltage toggle
- Side panel on asset click: properties, live chart, connection breadcrumbs

### Development Order
1. Backend foundations (JSON data model + FastAPI skeleton)
2. Simulation mock (engine pushing fake data)
3. Map integration (deferred — frontend)
4. Interaction layer (deferred — frontend)
5. Final polish (deferred — frontend)

